shelter in a Walmart.

00:01:22.601 --> 00:01:23.901
-Wow.
-Then my 15th birthday,

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:25.300
we rented out Dave &amp; Busters.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:28.067
16th birthday,
we rented out Six Flags.

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:29.634
17th birthday was quarantine.

00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:31.601
18th birthday was Disney World.

00:01:31.601 --> 00:01:33.767
And 19th birthday
was "The Tonight Show"!

00:01:33.767 --> 00:01:35.400
-That's exactly how you do it!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.701
Come on, now.

00:01:36.701 --> 00:01:38.467
-This is the best one.
-That's how you do it.

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:40.100
-This is the best one, for sure.
-I'm wishing you the best.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.334
We're sending you the vibes.
-Thank you.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.634
-You're gonna have
the best year ever.

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:45.267
You -- at 19, you've already
accomplished so much.

00:01:45.267 --> 00:01:47.734
You're one of Time's 100
Most Influential People.

00:01:47.734 --> 00:01:49.167
Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:50.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:52.634
-"Boomerang" has almost
1 billion views on YouTube.

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:54.067
-Wild.
-A billion.

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:57.100
-A billion. And it just had its
six-year anniversary, too.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.367
-Isn't that wild?

00:01:58.367 --> 00:01:59.667
-It's crazy to think about.
-One billion views.

00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:03.133
-And it still gets about
500,000 views a day.

00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:04.801
-Wow.
-Which is wild to think about.

00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:07.033
And like, little kids now,
who are 2 years old,

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:09.067
their favorite song
is "Boomerang."

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:10.234
And for me, I'm like, "How?

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:11.534
They weren't even alive
when it came out."

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:12.701
It's wild.
-Wow.

00:02:12.701 --> 00:02:14.200
It just lives on.
But there's -- there's one thing

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.868
that you haven't done yet,
and it involves Lady Gaga.

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:19.100
-Oh, yes.
-Explain this to me.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:22.067
-So, my, like, dream
is to either, like,

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:25.100
play Lady Gaga in a biopic
of her life one day.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.767
-Uh-huh.
-Now, if that doesn't happen,

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:29.067
my next dream is to just be
a backup dancer for her --

00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:30.501
for one day.
-Well, I mean, you --

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:31.534
-One day.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:33.033
-You can do it. I mean --
-Thank you.

00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:35.934
We actually -- we have the same
choreographer, Richy Jackson,

00:02:35.934 --> 00:02:38.334
who is amazing.
And I -- I tell him

00:02:38.334 --> 00:02:41.868
all the time, because I know
about 20, 25 Lady Gaga dances

00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:43.601
that she does at her concerts.

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:46.701
And I tell Richy all the time,
I'm like, "Listen, one day,

00:02:46.701 --> 00:02:49.033
a dancer's gonna be sick,
they're not gonna be on stage,

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:50.667
you're gonna have one hour
to find someone

00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:52.934
who knows the whole set,
and you're gonna call me,

00:02:52.934 --> 00:02:54.334
and I'm gonna be prepared."

00:02:54.334 --> 00:02:57.100
And I -- I'm banking on that
happening one day.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.868
-I mean -- Lady Gaga watches
the show all the time.

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:00.934
Gaga...
-Gaga...

00:03:00.934 --> 00:03:02.133
-Hello, come on, let's go.

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:03.334
This is it, right now.
-Gaga.

00:03:03.334 --> 00:03:04.701
-A dream.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:07.501
Don't stop a dream.
Don't stop a dream.

00:03:07.501 --> 00:03:11.701
-One day.
It can be a press stunt --

00:03:11.701 --> 00:03:13.667
for me.
-Yeah.

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:15.467
Whatever, whoever you want it
to be, yeah.

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:16.634
We've got to do it.

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:17.868
I would love to see you.
Come on.

00:03:17.868 --> 00:03:20.601
-Hey, Gaga, Jimmy said --
-She's -- I mean, yeah.

00:03:20.601 --> 00:03:22.334
[ Laughter ]
She's touring now, right?

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:24.033
Is Gaga doing --
-Yeah, "Chromatica Ball"

00:03:24.033 --> 00:03:25.167
is just about to start.
-Yes.

00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:27.067
-Yeah.
-It's happening.

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:28.634
All right,
I'm gonna vibe this out.

00:03:28.634 --> 00:03:29.801
This is the golden birthday.
Come on.

00:03:29.801 --> 00:03:30.968
If we all send the vibes,
it's gonna happen.

00:03:30.968 --> 00:03:32.234
-Right! You would think,
you would think.

00:03:32.234 --> 00:03:33.667
-All right, good, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:35.834
I want to talk to you about
"So You Think You Can Dance."

00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:37.567
-Yes.
-Season 17 premiered last night.

00:03:37.567 --> 00:03:39.567
You are a judge.
-Yes, yes.

00:03:39.567 --> 00:03:41.734
-I -- how -- You've been a fan
of the show, must have been,

00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:43.968
since you were a baby.
-Yeah, since I --

00:03:43.968 --> 00:03:45.601
I mean, the show came out,
I think,

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:47.100
the year after I was born.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.367
So it's been around
literally my whole life.

00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:49.868
-Literally when you were a baby,
yeah.

00:03:49.868 --> 00:03:52.200
-Yeah, which is -- it --
it's crazy to think about.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.667
I remember going to
the tour of the show, actually,

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.200
when I was like 5,
and I did the meet-and-greet

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.534
with the cast of that season --

00:03:57.534 --> 00:03:59.801
I think it was season nine
maybe at the time.

00:03:59.801 --> 00:04:01.901
And it was -- No,
it definitely wasn't season 9.

00:04:01.901 --> 00:04:03.434
It was season 5.
'Cause my friend

00:04:03.434 --> 00:04:06.033
was on season -- anyways,
back at it -- it was season 5.

00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:10.067
And it -- it's just so cool
to think that this show

00:04:10.067 --> 00:04:12.267
is such an iconic piece

00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:15.200
of the dance world
and of dance history.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:19.701
And every dancer
that has such a household name

00:04:19.701 --> 00:04:21.734
was born on this show,
if that makes sense.

00:04:21.734 --> 00:04:23.000
-Yeah.
-They were first seen

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.968
on this show, and it gives
dancers such a platform.

00:04:24.968 --> 00:04:27.667
And so, to be part of it
in this way, just --

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.100
It means the world to me.
-Do they --

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.734
Do they get nervous when they go
out and dance in front of you?

00:04:31.734 --> 00:04:34.100
-Oh, my God, they're terrified.
-Yeah, of course.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:37.100
-They're terrified.
And it's -- it's funny to watch,

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:38.901
because being on the judges
side of the things --

00:04:38.901 --> 00:04:40.234
You know, I had
"Dancing With the Stars,"

00:04:40.234 --> 00:04:42.234
where I was competing.
I competed on "Masked Singer."

00:04:42.234 --> 00:04:43.434
I was
"Ultimate Dance Competition."

00:04:43.434 --> 00:04:46.167
I've had my fair share
of elimination shows.

00:04:46.167 --> 00:04:48.267
And to be on this side of it,
be judging,

00:04:48.267 --> 00:04:49.701
it's interesting to watch.

00:04:49.701 --> 00:04:53.133
It's like "They're nervous,
but I'm not, so why are they?"

00:04:53.133 --> 00:04:54.634
But then I'm like,
"No, okay, now I --"

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:56.434
-"I've been on the other side,"
yeah, where you were nervous,

00:04:56.434 --> 00:04:57.767
and, yeah, and being judged.
-Yeah.

00:04:57.767 --> 00:04:59.968
They are so talented, though,
it's insane.

00:04:59.968 --> 00:05:01.834
-How do you --
How are you as a judge?

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:04.534
-How do you think I am?
-I would say that you're --

00:05:04.534 --> 00:05:06.234
I would say that you're --
You give positive --

00:05:06.234 --> 00:05:08.467
I think you're always positive
when I'm around you,

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:10.968
so I would say you probably
give positive feedback.

00:05:10.968 --> 00:05:12.501
I mean, I don't know
if I could do it,

00:05:12.501 --> 00:05:14.868
because I'd be like --
"I don't know."

00:05:14.868 --> 00:05:16.734
I would be like,
"I don't -- pass."

00:05:16.734 --> 00:05:18.801
-I'll admit I'm --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.801 --> 00:05:20.234
-"Go talk to someone else.
Talk to another judge."

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:21.834
-"Next, next."
-Yeah, yeah, I can't do it.

00:05:21.834 --> 00:05:24.601
-I will admit,
I am the honest judge.

00:05:24.601 --> 00:05:26.067
So, if something is great,

00:05:26.067 --> 00:05:27.667
I can't hold back,
I will tell you.

00:05:27.667 --> 00:05:28.968
-Yep.
-If something is not,

00:05:28.968 --> 00:05:30.968
I will also not hold back,
and I will tell you.

00:05:30.968 --> 00:05:33.801
So it can be a problem
sometimes.

00:05:33.801 --> 00:05:36.367
But I just --
I want the people who are good

00:05:36.367 --> 00:05:38.601
to know that I am dead serious
when they are good.

00:05:38.601 --> 00:05:39.767
You know what I mean?
I don't just want

00:05:39.767 --> 00:05:41.067
to tell everyone
that they're great, if...

00:05:41.067 --> 00:05:43.734
-Yeah, of course.
-...you know, they're not.

00:05:43.734 --> 00:05:45.400
-Yeah. You go,
"Hey, you got to work --"

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:46.667
-I don't know.
-"You got to work harder."

00:05:46.667 --> 00:05:48.033
-I'm naturally
just an honest person.

00:05:48.033 --> 00:05:49.300
-Yeah.
-All the time.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:50.734
-I think that people would
rather hear that, though,

00:05:50.734 --> 00:05:52.267
and go, like, "Hey, come back."
-Yeah.

00:05:52.267 --> 00:05:53.801
-"Go work on this.
You have something,

00:05:53.801 --> 00:05:55.067
if you want to do this."
-Exactly.

00:05:55.067 --> 00:05:56.300
Exactly.
That's what we tell people.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:57.667
We say, "Go, and come back,
and keep working."

00:05:57.667 --> 00:06:01.033
Because everybody who gets
to this point is incredible.

00:06:01.033 --> 00:06:04.234
-Yeah, and if you hear something
from JoJo Siwa, to give you

00:06:04.234 --> 00:06:07.501
even any advice, or any help,
you'll never forget that

00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:08.734
as long as you live.
-Yes.

00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:09.901
-You'll go,
"Yeah, she told me to do that,

00:06:09.901 --> 00:06:11.300
and I'm gonna do that."
-Thank you.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:13.667
-I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's the birthday girl,

00:06:13.667 --> 00:06:15.767
JoJo Siwa in
"So You Think You Can Dance."

00:06:15.767 --> 00:06:17.067
Take a look at this.

00:06:17.067 --> 00:06:19.367
-Out of everyone
that I've seen today,

00:06:19.367 --> 00:06:21.834
you had the most fun
on this stage.

00:06:21.834 --> 00:06:23.367
And that is something
that I really appreciate.

00:06:23.367 --> 00:06:24.734
-Thank you.

00:06:24.734 --> 00:06:28.000
-I love that you are
who you are.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:31.167
I love that you're out here in
heels and your little shorts.

00:06:31.167 --> 00:06:32.534
I'm...
-You know it.

00:06:32.534 --> 00:06:34.400
-...a hundred --
My best --

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:36.067
[ Laughter and cheers ]

00:06:36.067 --> 00:06:37.934
Listen.

00:06:37.934 --> 00:06:40.167
I am very gay, too.

00:06:40.167 --> 00:06:44.100
So I --
Yes, whatever you do, you do.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:47.167
Not my type.
But my --

00:06:47.167 --> 00:06:48.501
-Don't worry.
You're not mine, either.

00:06:48.501 --> 00:06:51.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:51.167 --> 00:06:52.801
-He was amazing.
-Nailed it. That's good.

00:06:52.801 --> 00:06:54.801
-That was Beau. He's great.
-He's great?

00:06:54.801 --> 00:06:57.467
JoJo Siwa, everybody.
"So You Think You Can Dance"

00:06:57.467 --> 00:07:00.634
airs Wednesday nights
at 9:00 p.m. on Fox.

